Z||000005||RossT||08-22-2000||11:47 PM||||The Peace Gargens are a massive flower garden on the border of Canada and US.  Half in Canada and half in the us. It covers several acres.  No barb wire fence on this border area.  Suppose to show  goodwill between the two countries, or something mushy like that.<P>Mr. Fiero, your plates are reall good looking with the green and white, Will you be able to keep them when you switch to the new "blue plates" that colorado is isueing??<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 08-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfiero||08-23-2000||12:28 AM||||Ross,<P>Colorado is keeping the green and white colors, just reversed.  The "old" style is white with green mountains, and the "new" style is green with white/gray mountains.  <P>There are some with blue mountains, but those are dealer plates (for demos, etc.).<P><BR>Even so, I will probably "lose" my plates when it's time to get the new ones (I have to have a souvenir!)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||5
